    <ImplementationPlan>
      <T-001><Title>kafedra-flow-intake: reduce lifecycle navigation to one desktop action</Title><DependsOn></DependsOn><AcceptanceCriteria><Criterion>The register exposes current/archive as one persistent mutually exclusive desktop state.</Criterion><Criterion>Switching preserves search and ordinary filters and never changes persisted lifecycle.</Criterion><Criterion>An absent selected plan cannot leave stale detail visible.</Criterion></AcceptanceCriteria><Verification><Command>node --test tests/lifecycle.test.mjs</Command></Verification></T-001>
      <T-002><Title>kafedra-design: specify a stable desktop segmented control</Title><DependsOn><T-001/></DependsOn><AcceptanceCriteria><Criterion>The segment is permanently visible, separate from general filters and uses existing tokens.</Criterion><Criterion>Text, shape, aria-selected and visible focus express selection independently of color.</Criterion><Criterion>Targets are at least 44 pixels; no mobile-specific mode is introduced.</Criterion></AcceptanceCriteria><Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification></T-002>
      <T-003><Title>kafedra-motion: choose no-motion for lifecycle switching</Title><DependsOn><T-002/></DependsOn><AcceptanceCriteria><Criterion>Semantic state, request and list replacement happen immediately without animation dependency.</Criterion><Criterion>`prefers-reduced-motion` produces the same complete static behavior and no mobile-only transition is added.</Criterion></AcceptanceCriteria><Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification></T-003>
      <T-004><Title>kafedra-feature: install the desktop segment over the existing lifecycle authority</Title><DependsOn><T-003/></DependsOn><AcceptanceCriteria><Criterion>The visible select is replaced by one tablist while the select remains only as an inaccessible compatibility bridge.</Criterion><Criterion>Click and keyboard actions reuse the existing status-filtered fetch path.</Criterion><Criterion>Current/archive empty states are distinct and secondary filters remain authoritative.</Criterion></AcceptanceCriteria><Verification><Command>node --test tests/plans-lifecycle-desktop.test.mjs</Command></Verification></T-004>
      <T-005><Title>kafedra-design-audit: inspect actual desktop hierarchy, focus and empty states</Title><DependsOn><T-004/></DependsOn><AcceptanceCriteria><Criterion>The independent audit returns PASS, REVISE or BLOCK with desktop evidence.</Criterion><Criterion>No blocker remains in hierarchy, focus, selected semantics, static state or narrowed-window compatibility.</Criterion></AcceptanceCriteria><Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification></T-005>
      <T-006><Title>kafedra-tests: prove one-action desktop filtering and compatibility</Title><DependsOn><T-005/></DependsOn><AcceptanceCriteria><Criterion>Unit tests cover state bridge, keyboard behavior, empty copy, no persistence and target size.</Criterion><Criterion>Desktop Playwright covers current/archive server query, preserved search, stale-detail reset and visible focus.</Criterion><Criterion>Full project CI remains green.</Criterion></AcceptanceCriteria><Verification><Command>npm test</Command><Command>npx playwright test tests/browser/plans-lifecycle-desktop.spec.mjs --project=desktop</Command></Verification></T-006>
      <T-007><Title>kafedra-release: exact-head merge, post-merge and terminal archive</Title><DependsOn><T-006/></DependsOn><AcceptanceCriteria><Criterion>Every required check succeeds on one unchanged PR head before squash merge.</Criterion><Criterion>Post-merge CI succeeds before a separate archive-only applied transition.</Criterion></AcceptanceCriteria><Verification><Command>npm run check</Command><Command>npm run docs:check</Command><Command>npm test</Command></Verification></T-007>
